Package: bkmborrow
Type: Package
Title: Dynamic Historical Borrowing for Bayesian Kaplan-Meier Inference
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Yusuke", "Yamaguchi", email = "yamagubed@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements dynamic borrowing of historical survival data within
    the conjugate Bayesian Kaplan-Meier framework, in which daily discrete
    hazards receive independent beta priors. Historical event and event-free
    counts are discounted by arm-specific weights determined from the
    discrepancy in restricted mean survival time (RMST) between the historical
    and current trials. The weight's tuning constant can be set from a
    clinically elicited tolerance in days. Exact posterior moments of the
    RMST, posterior sampling, and simulation-based calibration of the
    posterior-probability decision threshold for type I error control are
    provided. Historical data may be available for the control arm only, the
    treatment arm only, or both arms.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports: stats
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), parallel
